- AI consultant: HTTPX and HTTPCore (BSD-3-Clause), Pydantic (MIT),
  certifi (MPL-2.0), python-dotenv (BSD-3-Clause). Exact versions are pinned
  in backend/requirements.txt. No LLM weights are bundled; the configured
  provider supplies its own model and applicable license. LLM calls are
  made only to the configured LLM_BASE_URL; no Ollama instance or LLM weights
  are installed by this project. PostgreSQL uses the PostgreSQL License;
  psycopg uses LGPL-3.0. SQLite remains available for Python development.

Synthetic/local data:
- The five UI images in frontend/public/images were generated using built-in ImageGen
  for this project. Prompts are recorded in docs/design/assets-prompts.json.
  Original files are bundled locally; no external image service is needed at runtime.
- User profiles, company details, product terms and articles in api/demo_data.py are synthetic demo data.
- Product rates are illustrative; no current central-bank or commercial-bank feed is connected.
- The developer-supplied ml/ service includes a trained LightGBM model and a
  synthetic-data training script. Its source, dependencies and model artifact
  are consumed unchanged by Django through an internal HTTP adapter.
- ML components: LightGBM (MIT), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), FastAPI (MIT),
  Pydantic (MIT), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause). Original dependency ranges remain in ml/requirements.txt; deploy/ml-constraints.txt
  pins the verified Linux environment without modifying ml/. CI runs real inference.
- EGRUL/EGRIP/FNS/BKI are explicit local synthetic fixtures. No paid APIs are used.
- Offers, file exchange, local PDF contracts, simulated signing and disbursement
  are implemented. No real financial or legal operations are performed.
- PDF dependencies: ReportLab (BSD), pypdf (BSD-3-Clause), Pillow (MIT-CMU),
  charset-normalizer (MIT). DejaVu Sans (Bitstream Vera / DejaVu terms) is
  installed from Debian fonts-dejavu-core in backend images.
- ML transitive dependencies include SciPy (BSD-3-Clause), Starlette (BSD-3-Clause),
  AnyIO (MIT), uvloop (MIT/Apache-2.0), httptools (MIT), watchfiles (MIT),
  websockets (BSD-3-Clause), python-dotenv (BSD-3-Clause); see pinned constraints.
- No third-party customer dataset is used; the supplied model and its generator
  use synthetic data. Real borrower quality and calibration are not established.
- Original task documents and the HTML prototype were supplied by the project owner;
  third-party names and trademarks remain the property of their respective owners.
